course: dictionary
lesson: 1121
title: A word with a clue inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words can be split into smaller words you already know. Breadwinner is made of bread and winner. Bread can mean food, and a winner is someone who gets something, so the word hints at someone who brings in food and money. Context helps you check it.
explain: The clue comes from the sentence «Berdiansk has a monument to the goby, the Goby Breadwinner, that fed people in hard years.» Something that fed people in hard years kept them going, so a breadwinner provides what a family needs to live.
explain: Now the family meaning. A breadwinner is the person in a family who earns the money the family lives on. Today many families have two breadwinners, or a mum who is the main one. Test it by swapping in «the person who earns the money» and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A breadwinner is the person in a family who earns the money the family lives on.
fact: Bread here means money and food, which is why the word sounds like it is about baking.
fact: Breadwinner is a noun, and its plural is breadwinners.
fact: Today many families have two breadwinners, or a mum who is the main one.
fact: The Goby Breadwinner is a monument in Berdiansk, made to honour the goby, a small fish that fed people in hard years.
exercise: In a family, what is the breadwinner? | The house where the family lives | *The person who earns the money the family lives on | The baker who sells the bread | The oldest child who does the cooking
exercise: Find the two smaller words hidden in breadwinner. | read and winner | bed and winner | bread and wind | *bread and winner
exercise: Today a mum and a dad both go out to work and earn money. Can both be breadwinners? | *Yes, both can be breadwinners | No, only a fish can be a breadwinner | No, breadwinners are always children | No, only the dad can be
test: Which sentence uses breadwinner correctly? | The breadwinner was the sunny weather at the seaside | Breadwinner means very old | I ate a breadwinner for lunch | *My dad is the breadwinner, because he earns the money our family lives on
test: In «the Goby Breadwinner, that fed people in hard years», what does fed mean? | *Kept people alive by giving them food | Painted people in bright colours | Argued with people | Ran away from people
exam: Using the clues in «bread» and «winner», and the sentence «Today in many families both parents are breadwinners», what does breadwinner mean? | A person who bakes bread for the shop | *A person who earns the money the family lives on | A person who wins every race | A person who never has any food
